{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"saintly-creeded-gecko","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Observation\nOn 2026-11-11 a live agentic run of `us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0` on Bedrock (us-west-2) with rebar's default `max_tokens` (`DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS = 16000`, src/rebar/llm/config.py:111) was rejected before generation: HTTP 400 ValidationException \"The maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 8192\". The same run with `max_tokens=8192` completed.\nSo every rebar LLM operation on Maverick fails unless the operator lowers `max_tokens`, and nothing in rebar tells them the model's limit. Other Bedrock models with output caps below 16000 are likely affected the same way; not surveyed.\nFound while fixing garlicky-leery-seal.\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A rebar run on a model whose output cap is below the configured max_tokens either sends a value within the cap or fails with an error naming the cap and the setting to change.\n","id":"afe0-e7c9-5df2-49e9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Default llm max_tokens 16000 exceeds Llama 4 Maverick's 8192 limit on Bedrock"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794466773468852001,"uuid":"ef85224c-e393-4318-876a-3bd242b1fe4e"}